BT /F1 10 Tf 28 666.6 Td (1. What is the term for an object, material, substance, condition, process, or behavior that can cause harm?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 653.6 Td (Answer: hazard \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 634.6 Td (2. What acronym refers to the organization or department responsible for reviewing legislation, developing safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 621.6 Td (programs, and providing guidance in identifying hazards?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 608.6 Td (Answer: EH&S \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 589.6 Td (3. What type of control involves changing the way people work through training, policies, or design changes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 576.6 Td (Answer: administrative controls \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 557.6 Td (4. What should be provided to protect workers from inhaling toxic gases?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 544.6 Td (Answer: Respirators \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 525.6 Td (5. What posture-related practice helps prevent injury by using leg muscles instead of back muscles when lifting?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 512.6 Td (Answer: Proper Lifting technique \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 493.6 Td (6. What program monitors the health of staff and students exposed to hazardous materials?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 480.6 Td (Answer: Medical surveillance \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 461.6 Td (7. What type of control involves isolating people from hazards by replacing equipment or changing the work environment?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 448.6 Td (Answer: Engineering Controls \227 Correct) Tj ET
